const e=[{community_id:0,name:"Physically-Based & Differentiable Rendering",tagline:"Monte Carlo light transport, inverse and neural appearance.",description:"The classical rendering core, updated for the differentiable era. Papers advance unbiased Monte Carlo estimators, physically-based BRDF/BSDF and SVBRDF appearance, and differentiable/inverse rendering that recovers scene parameters by backpropagating through light transport. A strong sub-thread brings neural decoders and caches into real-time rendering without abandoning physical correctness.",methods:["Monte Carlo path/light transport","Differentiable & inverse rendering","BRDF/BSDF & SVBRDF appearance modeling","Reservoir resampling (ReSTIR)","Neural appearance decoders & caches","Walk-on-spheres / grid-free PDE estimators"],key_contribution:"Made rendering differentiable and partly real-time while keeping Monte Carlo light transport as the fidelity reference.",exemplars:[{ay:"Zeltner 2023",doi:"10.1145/3659577"},{ay:"Bangaru 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555397"},{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618331"},{ay:"Rioux-Lavoie 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555450"},{ay:"Zhou 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555403"}]},{community_id:1,name:"Elastodynamics, Contact & Cloth Simulation",tagline:"Stable solvers for deformable solids, contact, and cloth.",description:"Despite its keyword-derived 'geometry processing' placeholder, this community is really physics-based simulation of deformable bodies. It centers on robust implicit integrators, intersection-free contact via incremental potential contact (IPC), and cloth dynamics, with adjacent work on differentiable solvers, inverse material design, and computational fabrication (multi-axis 3D-print slicing).",methods:["Implicit Euler / variational integrators","Incremental Potential Contact (IPC) & barriers","Projective / position-based dynamics","Finite-element & mesh-free elasticity","Differentiable simulation for inverse design","Neural cloth & material models"],key_contribution:"Delivered fast, unconditionally stable, intersection-free solvers (VBD, GIPC) that became practical workhorses for contact-rich simulation.",exemplars:[{ay:"Chen 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658179"},{ay:"Huang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3643028"},{ay:"Modi 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658184"},{ay:"Bertiche 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555491"},{ay:"Feng 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555464"}]},{community_id:2,name:"Generative 3D: Text-to-Shape & Texturing",tagline:"Turning text, images, and 2D priors into 3D assets.",description:"This cluster (mislabeled 'cages/barycentric') is the text-to-3D and 3D-generation community. It grows from zero-shot text-to-mesh via CLIP to large-scale controllable generators of geometry and PBR materials, plus text/image-driven 3D editing, expandable scene synthesis, and multi-view diffusion texturing. Pretrained 2D priors are repurposed as engines for 3D content.",methods:["Text-to-3D via CLIP / 2D diffusion priors","Large-scale 3D geometry+material generators","Score-distillation & multi-view diffusion texturing","Latent tri-plane / neural-field 3D generation","Text- and image-prompted 3D editing"],key_contribution:"Scaled 3D asset generation from zero-shot text-to-mesh (CLIP-Mesh) to controllable production-grade geometry and materials (CLAY).",exemplars:[{ay:"Zhang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658146"},{ay:"Khalid 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555392"},{ay:"Zhuang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3610548.3618190"},{ay:"Wu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658188"},{ay:"He 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658147"}]},{community_id:3,name:"Diffusion Models for Image & Video Generation",tagline:"Controllable 2D synthesis, personalization, and video.",description:"The highest-impact generative community, built almost entirely on diffusion models. Work spans text-to-image personalization and concept extraction, appearance transfer, controllable text-to-video and image-to-video with explicit motion, low-light and restoration, and fast single-step synthesis via adversarial distillation. A notable strand folds inverse rendering into generation (RGB<->X).",methods:["Latent diffusion for image/video","Motion-conditioned & image-to-video generation","Subject/concept personalization","Adversarial diffusion distillation (few-step)","Cross-image attention & appearance transfer"],key_contribution:"Established diffusion as the default engine for controllable image and video generation, with explicit motion control and near-real-time distillation.",exemplars:[{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657518"},{ay:"Shi 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657497"},{ay:"Ma 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657469"},{ay:"Zeng 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657445"},{ay:"Yang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657481"}]},{community_id:4,name:"Radiance Fields & Gaussian Splatting",tagline:"From NeRF to explicit, real-time Gaussian primitives.",description:"The center of gravity of the era and the most-cited community. It pivots from implicit neural radiance fields to explicit 3D/2D Gaussian splatting for high-quality, real-time novel-view synthesis, then races to fix splatting's weaknesses: geometric accuracy via surfels and opacity fields, dynamic 4D scenes, city-scale hierarchies, memory/compute reduction, view-consistent sorting, and ray-traced particles.",methods:["3D/2D Gaussian Splatting","Neural radiance fields & neural voxels","Dynamic / 4D scene representations","Gaussian surfels & opacity fields for surfaces","Level-of-detail & compression for large scenes","Gaussian ray tracing"],key_contribution:"Made photoreal novel-view synthesis real-time and editable through explicit Gaussian primitives, led by 2D Gaussian Splatting.",exemplars:[{ay:"Huang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657428"},{ay:"Fang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555383"},{ay:"Jiang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657448"},{ay:"Duan 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657463"},{ay:"Dai 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657441"}]},{community_id:5,name:"Character Animation & Human Motion",tagline:"Physics-based control and generative human motion.",description:"Character animation and human-motion synthesis, split between physics-based control and kinematic generation. Physics-based work learns reinforcement-learned controllers and discrete motion representations for versatile, scene-aware character control; the generative side uses transformers and diffusion for motion in-betweening, co-speech gesture, human-object interaction, and real-time reconstruction from sparse sensors.",methods:["Reinforcement-learned physics controllers","Motion diffusion & in-betweening","Discrete/VQ motion representations","Sparse-IMU / sparse-sensor motion tracking","Co-speech gesture & human-object interaction"],key_contribution:"Unified versatile character control (masked motion inpainting, scalable discrete motion) and brought diffusion to human-motion generation.",exemplars:[{ay:"Li 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618333"},{ay:"Tessler 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Jiang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555428"},{ay:"Yao 2023",doi:"10.1145/3658137"},{ay:"Cohan 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657414"}]},{community_id:6,name:"Head Avatars & Facial Animation",tagline:"Photoreal, drivable heads and speech-driven faces.",description:"Digital-human faces and heads: reconstructing personalized, animatable head avatars and driving them from video or speech. The community moves from morphable meshes and facial NeRFs to Gaussian point-based heads and blendshapes, with a strong speech-driven strand (lip-sync, emotional and stylistic facial animation via diffusion) and GAN/NeRF-based face editing.",methods:["Facial NeRF & morphable models","Gaussian point-based / codec head avatars","Speech-driven facial animation (diffusion)","Talking-head lip-sync & video editing","Portrait relighting & face editing"],key_contribution:"Advanced drivable, photoreal head avatars from facial NeRFs to real-time Gaussian heads, with expressive speech-driven animation.",exemplars:[{ay:"Gao 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555501"},{ay:"Chen 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657499"},{ay:"Sun 2023",doi:"10.1145/3658221"},{ay:"Ma 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657462"},{ay:"Cheng 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555399"}]},{community_id:7,name:"Geometry Processing: Surfaces, SDFs & CAD",tagline:"Reconstruction, implicit surfaces, and B-rep/CAD generation.",description:"The genuine geometry-processing community (not 'faces/performance capture'). It covers surface reconstruction from point clouds via implicit and statistical methods, signed/unsigned distance fields and winding numbers, robust mesh Booleans and simplification, and a fast-growing generative-CAD strand producing editable B-rep models and 3D shapes with diffusion.",methods:["Implicit surface reconstruction (SDF/UDF)","Neural Galerkin & statistical Poisson reconstruction","Winding numbers & normal orientation","Robust mesh Booleans & simplification","Generative B-rep / CAD diffusion"],key_contribution:"Pushed robust surface reconstruction and brought generative diffusion to structured, editable CAD (BrepGen).",exemplars:[{ay:"Xu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658129"},{ay:"Hui 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555394"},{ay:"Sellán 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555441"},{ay:"Huang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555457"},{ay:"Cherchi 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555460"}]},{community_id:8,name:"Fluid Simulation & Flow Maps",tagline:"Flow-map, vortex, and reduced-order fluid solvers.",description:"Physics-based fluid and continuum simulation, distinguished from the elastodynamics cluster by its focus on flow. The signature contribution is the flow-map paradigm - neural and particle flow maps for accurate long-range advection - alongside vortex/impulse methods, SPH surface tension, hybrid Lagrangian/Eulerian solvers, and neural reduced-order models for elastoplasticity and fracture.",methods:["Flow-map (neural & particle) advection","Vortex / impulse / covector methods","Hybrid Lagrangian-Eulerian (PIC/APIC) solvers","SPH & surface-tension flows","Neural reduced-order modeling"],key_contribution:"Introduced the flow-map paradigm for high-accuracy long-range advection in incompressible fluid simulation.",exemplars:[{ay:"Zhou 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658180"},{ay:"Deng 2023",doi:""},{ay:"Zong 2023",doi:""},{ay:"Xing 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555476"},{ay:"Jeske 2023",doi:"10.1145/3631936"}]},{community_id:9,name:"Computational Displays, Cameras & Perception",tagline:"Holography, computational optics, and perceptual metrics.",description:"Work at the hardware-perception boundary. It spans computer-generated holography and holographic near-eye displays, co-designed computational cameras and lenses, VR/AR display power and perception, and perceptual quality metrics and sampling. The unifying theme is optimizing the full imaging pipeline - optics, display, and the human visual system - together.",methods:["Computer-generated holography","End-to-end / co-designed optics & cameras","Perceptual quality metrics (VDP)","VR/AR display power & perception studies","Blue-noise & optimal-transport sampling"],key_contribution:"Jointly optimized optics, displays, and perception - from brighter multi-color holograms to color-and-video perceptual metrics.",exemplars:[{ay:"Kim 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658168"},{ay:"Chakravarthula 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555508"},{ay:"Duinkharjav 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555473"},{ay:"Kavaklı 2023",doi:"10.1145/3610548.3618135"},{ay:"Mantiuk 2024",doi:""}]},{community_id:10,name:"Clothed Human Avatars & Garment Capture",tagline:"Dressing, capturing, and animating clothed humans.",description:"Full-body clothed-human avatars and garments, sitting between digital humans and cloth simulation. Work captures body-and-clothing from monocular video, recovers or programs sewing patterns, digitizes humans from a single image with diffusion priors, and represents drivable clothed avatars with layered Gaussian and codec representations for telepresence and try-on.",methods:["Monocular body-and-clothing capture","Sewing-pattern reconstruction & programming","Single-image human digitization (diffusion)","Layered Gaussian / codec clothed avatars","Physically-simulated clothing appearance"],key_contribution:"Disentangled body and clothing for capture, try-on, and drivable clothed avatars, including layered Gaussian representations.",exemplars:[{ay:"Feng 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555423"},{ay:"Liu 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618319"},{ay:"Korosteleva 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618351"},{ay:"Lin 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657501"},{ay:"Xiang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555456"}]},{community_id:11,name:"Intrinsic Images, Relighting & Compositing",tagline:"Albedo, shading, and illumination for image editing.",description:"A compact but high-impact community on intrinsic image decomposition, inverse rendering, relighting, and realistic compositing. It separates photographs into albedo, shading, and illumination - moving from optimization and differentiable Monte Carlo inverse rendering to ordinal-shading decomposition and diffusion-based intrinsic layers - to enable illumination-aware editing, harmonization, and shadow/relighting control.",methods:["Intrinsic image decomposition (ordinal shading)","Differentiable Monte Carlo inverse rendering","Diffusion-based intrinsic layers & normals","Relighting & light-source control","Shadow removal & compositing harmonization"],key_contribution:"Advanced in-the-wild intrinsic decomposition and relighting from optimization toward robust diffusion-based estimation.",exemplars:[{ay:"Careaga 2023",doi:"10.1145/3630750"},{ay:"Zhu 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555407"},{ay:"Luo 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657472"},{ay:"Careaga 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Li 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555384"}]},{community_id:12,name:"Fast Median Filtering Algorithms",tagline:"High-performance, classical image filtering.",description:"A small, tightly-focused island of classical algorithmics: fast median filtering for image processing. The papers develop constant-time, isotropic, and parallel-tiled median-filter algorithms that remove impulse noise while preserving edges - a reminder that non-learned, performance-oriented systems work still reaches the top venues.",methods:["Constant-time median filtering","Wavelet-matrix / histogram-based filters","Isotropic (non-square kernel) median filters","Hierarchical-tiling parallel algorithms"],key_contribution:"Delivered faster, isotropic, and parallel median-filtering algorithms with strong asymptotic and practical performance.",exemplars:[{ay:"Moroto 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555512"},{ay:"Weiss 2025",doi:""},{ay:"Sugy 2025",doi:""}]}],i={title:"Generated and reconstructed assets are not simulation-ready",statement:"The neural-representation communities (radiance fields/splatting, generative image/video, generative 3D) and the physics-simulation communities (elastodynamics/contact, fluids) advanced in parallel with remarkably little cross-pollination. Assets that are generated or reconstructed with diffusion and Gaussian splatting are photoreal but not directly editable, riggable, or physically simulatable.",structural_evidence:"The youngest, most-cited clusters are neural: radiance fields/splatting (community 4, mean 60.5 citations), diffusion image/video (community 3, 53.3), and generative 3D (community 2, 25.5). The simulation clusters are older-rooted and lower-cited within this window (elastodynamics/contact 10.1, fluids 9.6). Bridging papers are rare and stand out precisely because they are exceptions - VR-GS (Jiang 2024) adds physical dynamics to Gaussian splats, Simplicits (Modi 2024) simulates any representation, and RGB<->X (Zeng 2024) folds inverse rendering into a generative model.",why_it_matters:"Production and interactive pipelines need a single asset that can be generated, relit, rigged, simulated, and animated. When generation and simulation live in separate representations, every generated asset requires expensive manual conversion (retopology, rigging, material authoring) before it can move, deform, or respond to contact.",what_would_resolve_it:"Shared, differentiable representations that are simultaneously renderable, editable, and simulatable - e.g., splatting or neural fields coupled to contact/elastodynamic solvers, structured/editable generative outputs (as BrepGen does for CAD), and benchmarks that reward physical plausibility and controllability, not only view synthesis quality."},a={claim:"Between 2022 and 2025, computer graphics reorganized around learned, differentiable scene representations - Gaussian splatting and diffusion priors - which now dominate reconstruction and content creation; yet the field's classical pillars (Monte Carlo light transport, contact-rich simulation, geometry processing) were not replaced but fused with, and still set the bar for, the neural turn.",evidence:[{point:"Gaussian splatting became the center of gravity for reconstruction and real-time rendering, the most-cited cluster in the corpus.",papers:[{ay:"Huang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657428"},{ay:"Kerbl 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Duan 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657463"}]},{point:"Diffusion priors took over 2D, 3D, and video content creation, from personalization to controllable video and large 3D-asset generation.",papers:[{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657518"},{ay:"Bar-Tal 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Zhang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658146"}]},{point:"The neural turn penetrated every subfield - avatars, garments, faces, and even CAD adopted Gaussian and diffusion representations.",papers:[{ay:"Chen 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657499"},{ay:"Lin 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657501"},{ay:"Xu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658129"}]},{point:"Differentiable and neural methods increasingly bridge rendering, appearance, and simulation rather than standing apart.",papers:[{ay:"Bangaru 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555397"},{ay:"Zeltner 2023",doi:"10.1145/3659577"},{ay:"Deng 2023",doi:""}]}],counter_evidence:[{point:"Classical Monte Carlo and physically-based rendering remain the fidelity gold standard and keep advancing (ReSTIR, differentiable path integrals).",papers:[{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618331"},{ay:"Zeltner 2023",doi:"10.1145/3659577"}]},{point:"The most-adopted simulation results of the era are first-principles solvers, not neural surrogates.",papers:[{ay:"Chen 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658179"},{ay:"Huang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3643028"}]},{point:"Some of the era's notable advances are purely algorithmic and non-learned - fluid flow-map solvers and fast median filtering.",papers:[{ay:"Zhou 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658180"},{ay:"Weiss 2025",doi:""}]}],gap:"The generative/neural clusters and the physics-simulation clusters barely cite each other, and generated assets are rarely simulation-ready or editable.",why_it_matters:"The field's next leap depends on unifying the two paradigms so a single asset can be generated, relit, simulated, and animated - otherwise photoreal neural content and controllable physical behavior stay in separate silos."},n=[{ay:"Huang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657428",community:4,modality:"2D Gaussian Splatting representation",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; corpus-topping 1514 citations",key_findings:"Flattens 3D Gaussians into oriented 2D disks to reconstruct geometrically accurate radiance fields, fixing the multi-view inconsistency of 3DGS while keeping real-time rendering.",limitations:"Surface accuracy still trades against appearance; thin structures and view-dependent effects remain challenging for planar primitives."},{ay:"Kerbl 2024",doi:"",community:4,modality:"Hierarchical 3DGS system",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; very large / city-scale scenes",key_findings:"A level-of-detail hierarchy of 3D Gaussians preserves visual quality while bounding training and rendering cost, enabling real-time rendering of very large captured scenes.",limitations:"Depends on high-quality large-scale capture; hierarchy construction and memory remain heavy for the largest scenes."},{ay:"Duan 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657463",community:4,modality:"4D dynamic Gaussian splatting",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; dynamic multi-view scenes",key_findings:"Represents dynamic scenes with 4D rotor-based Gaussians for efficient novel-view synthesis, handling sudden motion better than canonical-space-plus-deformation approaches.",limitations:"Dynamic capture and storage costs grow with sequence length; fast, complex motion still degrades fidelity."},{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657518",community:3,modality:"Video-diffusion motion controller",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 611 citations",key_findings:"MotionCtrl disentangles camera motion from object motion, giving unified, flexible control over both in text-to-video diffusion generation.",limitations:"Motion control fidelity depends on the base video model; fine object trajectories and long videos remain hard."},{ay:"Bar-Tal 2024",doi:"",community:3,modality:"Space-time video diffusion",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2024; 536 citations",key_findings:"Lumiere's Space-Time U-Net generates a video's full temporal extent in a single pass, improving global motion coherence over cascaded keyframe-then-interpolate pipelines.",limitations:"Whole-clip generation is compute-intensive and limited in duration/resolution; long-horizon consistency is still bounded."},{ay:"Sauer 2024",doi:"",community:3,modality:"Adversarial diffusion distillation",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2024; 302 citations",key_findings:"Latent adversarial diffusion distillation shifts high-resolution synthesis toward single-/few-step inference, greatly cutting sampling cost.",limitations:"Distillation can reduce diversity and fine detail; training is delicate and tied to the teacher model."},{ay:"Zhang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658146",community:2,modality:"Large-scale 3D generative model",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 512 citations",key_findings:"CLAY generates high-quality 3D geometry and PBR materials from diverse inputs, scaling controllable text-to-3D toward production-usable assets.",limitations:"Outputs are not inherently rigged/simulation-ready; controllability and fine structure still require downstream cleanup."},{ay:"Khalid 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555392",community:2,modality:"Zero-shot text-to-mesh (CLIP)",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 362 citations",key_findings:"CLIP-Mesh deforms a subdivided control mesh and its textures to match a text prompt with no 3D supervision, producing deployable textured meshes.",limitations:"Limited geometric detail and topology control; quality bounded by the CLIP prior and prone to artifacts."},{ay:"Wu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658188",community:2,modality:"Latent tri-plane 3D scene diffusion",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; blocks cropped from 3D scene meshes",key_findings:"BlockFusion generates 3D scenes as unit blocks and extrapolates new blocks to expand scenes seamlessly using hybrid tri-plane neural fields.",limitations:"Block boundaries and global scene coherence are hard to guarantee; training needs curated 3D scene data."},{ay:"Zeltner 2023",doi:"10.1145/3659577",community:0,modality:"Neural appearance model + system",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; real-time rendering system",key_findings:"Learned hierarchical textures decoded by neural networks reproduce complex, importance-sampled reflectance at real-time rates, previously reserved for offline rendering.",limitations:"Requires per-asset training/decoding; generality across arbitrary materials and lighting is still constrained."},{ay:"Bangaru 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555397",community:0,modality:"Differentiable neural-SDF rendering",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 50 citations",key_findings:"Computes correct gradients for neural SDF renderers via area-sampling reparameterization, handling silhouette discontinuities without explicit edge sampling.",limitations:"Focused on geometric parameters; cost and variance of the estimator grow with scene complexity."},{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618331",community:0,modality:"Physics-based inverse rendering (ReSTIR)",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2023; 48 citations",key_findings:"Amortizes samples across gradient steps using reservoir resampling, accelerating physics-based inverse rendering where the scene changes every optimization iteration.",limitations:"Demonstrated primarily for direct illumination; temporal reuse assumptions can bias fast-changing scenes."},{ay:"Chen 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658179",community:1,modality:"Physics solver (block coordinate descent)",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 43 citations",key_findings:"Vertex Block Descent solves implicit Euler via vertex-level Gauss-Seidel updates, achieving unconditional stability, high parallelism, and strong performance for deformable simulation.",limitations:"Gauss-Seidel convergence can slow on stiff, highly-coupled systems; global coupling and very high stiffness remain demanding."},{ay:"Huang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3643028",community:1,modality:"IPC contact optimization",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 38 citations",key_findings:"GIPC reformulates the IPC barrier for an efficient, robust Hessian approximation, giving fast, stable, intersection- and inversion-free contact via Gauss-Newton.",limitations:"Still an optimization per step; extreme contact density and friction accuracy add cost."},{ay:"Bertiche 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555491",community:1,modality:"Unsupervised neural cloth model",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 88 citations",key_findings:"Learns realistic cloth dynamics unsupervised from a physics-inspired formulation, generating garment animation without ground-truth simulation data.",limitations:"Generalization to unseen garments/materials and hard contact is limited compared to full physical solvers."},{ay:"Zhou 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658180",community:8,modality:"Particle flow-map fluid solver",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; incompressible fluids",key_findings:"Particle Flow Maps exploit particle trajectories as exact flow maps for accurate long-range advection in an Eulerian-Lagrangian framework, improving vorticity preservation.",limitations:"Bookkeeping of long trajectories adds cost; boundary handling and very turbulent regimes remain challenging."},{ay:"Deng 2023",doi:"",community:8,modality:"Neural flow-map fluid solver",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2023; 50 citations",key_findings:"Neural Flow Maps fuse spatially sparse neural fields with flow-map theory to reach state-of-the-art inviscid fluid simulation with strong vorticity preservation.",limitations:"Training/inference overhead of neural fields; accuracy depends on the sparse-field capacity and time-stepping."},{ay:"Zong 2023",doi:"",community:8,modality:"Neural reduced-order elastoplasticity",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2023; 43 citations",key_findings:"Neural Stress Fields provide a hybrid network-plus-physics reduced-order model for elastoplasticity and fracture, cutting the runtime and memory of full MPM.",limitations:"Reduced models trade accuracy for speed; extrapolation beyond training regimes and sharp fracture detail are limited."},{ay:"Li 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618333",community:5,modality:"Motion-diffusion for object interaction",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2023; 245 citations",key_findings:"Synthesizes full-body human motion for manipulating large objects, using object motion to guide plausible whole-body interaction.",limitations:"Depends on known object trajectories; contact accuracy and diverse object types remain constrained."},{ay:"Tessler 2024",doi:"",community:5,modality:"Physics-based character controller",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2024; 158 citations",key_findings:"MaskedMimic casts versatile physics-based control as masked motion inpainting, unifying keyframe, text, and scene control in one simulated controller.",limitations:"Requires large motion datasets and RL training; unseen tasks and precise contact still challenge the controller."},{ay:"Jiang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555428",community:5,modality:"Sparse-IMU motion reconstruction",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; six IMUs, real-time",key_findings:"Transformer Inertial Poser reconstructs full-body motion in real time from six IMUs while jointly generating terrain, addressing the under-determined sparse-sensor problem.",limitations:"Global translation drift and ambiguous poses persist; accuracy depends on learned motion priors."},{ay:"Gao 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555501",community:6,modality:"Semantic facial NeRF avatar",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 185 citations",key_findings:"Builds a disentangled, interpretable head NeRF driven by low-dimensional expression coefficients from monocular video, capturing hair and accessories.",limitations:"NeRF rendering is slow; extreme expressions and large view changes reduce fidelity."},{ay:"Chen 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657499",community:6,modality:"Gaussian point-based head avatar",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; monocular portrait video",key_findings:"MonoGaussianAvatar animates photoreal head avatars from monocular video using Gaussian point representations, improving speed over implicit head models.",limitations:"Monocular capture limits novel-view extrapolation; fine details like teeth and eyes remain hard."},{ay:"Sun 2023",doi:"10.1145/3658221",community:6,modality:"Speech-driven facial diffusion",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 122 citations",key_findings:"DiffPoseTalk uses diffusion to map speech to stylistic 3D facial animation and head pose, capturing the many-to-many speech-to-motion relationship and personal style.",limitations:"Style control needs reference data; long-range head-motion realism and lip precision are still limited."},{ay:"Xu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658129",community:7,modality:"Generative B-rep CAD diffusion",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 148 citations",key_findings:"BrepGen directly generates editable boundary-representation CAD models via diffusion over a structured latent tree of faces, edges, and vertices.",limitations:"Topological validity and complex constraint satisfaction are hard to guarantee; scales unevenly to intricate assemblies."},{ay:"Hui 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555394",community:7,modality:"Wavelet-domain shape diffusion",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 174 citations",key_findings:"Performs generative diffusion directly on a compact coarse/detail wavelet representation of truncated SDFs, enabling detailed 3D shape generation.",limitations:"Implicit outputs need meshing; sharp features and fine topology can be lost."},{ay:"Sellán 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555441",community:7,modality:"Statistical surface reconstruction",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 58 citations",key_findings:"Recasts Poisson surface reconstruction as a Gaussian process, yielding a statistical shape that supports likelihood queries about surface/interior membership.",limitations:"Added statistical machinery raises cost; very sparse or noisy inputs still limit certainty."},{ay:"Mantiuk 2024",doi:"",community:9,modality:"Perceptual video/image quality metric",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; 67 citations",key_findings:"ColorVideoVDP models spatial and temporal, luminance and chromatic vision to predict visible differences across image, video, and display distortions.",limitations:"Trained on specific viewing conditions; generalization to unseen displays and content types is bounded."},{ay:"Kim 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658168",community:9,modality:"Holographic near-eye display study",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; perceptual study",key_findings:"Shows that holographic parallax measurably improves perceived 3D realism in near-eye holographic displays, informing CGH supervision targets.",limitations:"Constrained by display hardware and étendue; results tied to the tested prototypes and conditions."},{ay:"Chakravarthula 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555508",community:9,modality:"Computer-generated holography",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 36 citations",key_findings:"Pupil-aware holography models the eye pupil to suppress speckle and improve perceived image quality in holographic displays with large étendue.",limitations:"Requires pupil tracking/assumptions; robustness to eye movement and hardware limits remains a challenge."},{ay:"Feng 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555423",community:10,modality:"Monocular body+clothing capture",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 125 citations",key_findings:"Separately models body and clothing from monocular video, enabling applications like virtual try-on that holistic avatar models cannot support.",limitations:"Loose garments and heavy occlusion reduce accuracy; monocular depth ambiguity persists."},{ay:"Liu 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618319",community:10,modality:"Single-image sewing-pattern recovery",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2023; SewFactory synthetic dataset",key_findings:"Recovers garment sewing patterns from a single daily photo, using a purpose-built synthetic dataset to bridge to real images.",limitations:"Sim-to-real gap and unusual garments limit accuracy; fine seam and material detail are approximate."},{ay:"Korosteleva 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618351",community:10,modality:"Programmatic garment patterns",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2023; 47 citations",key_findings:"GarmentCode expresses parametric sewing patterns as programs, bridging high-level construction goals and low-level editable pattern geometry.",limitations:"Programmatic authoring has a learning curve; expressive coverage of all garment styles is incremental."},{ay:"Careaga 2023",doi:"10.1145/3630750",community:11,modality:"Intrinsic image decomposition",n:"SIGGRAPH 2024; high-resolution decomposition",key_findings:"Ordinal-shading estimation decomposes images into accurate continuous shading and albedo at high resolution, improving inverse-rendering and compositing pipelines.",limitations:"Ill-posed separation still fails under strong colored illumination and complex interreflections."},{ay:"Zhu 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555407",community:11,modality:"Learning-based inverse rendering",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 109 citations",key_findings:"End-to-end inverse rendering with differentiable Monte Carlo raytracing recovers geometry, materials, and lighting of complex indoor scenes from a single image.",limitations:"Single-image ambiguity and global-illumination complexity cap accuracy for spatially-varying appearance."},{ay:"Careaga 2024",doi:"",community:11,modality:"Diffusion intrinsic decomposition",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2024; 57 citations",key_findings:"Separates images into diffuse albedo and colorful diffuse shading in the wild, relaxing the single-color-illumination and Lambertian assumptions of prior work.",limitations:"Specular and non-diffuse effects are not fully modeled; remains an under-constrained estimation."},{ay:"Weiss 2025",doi:"",community:12,modality:"Median-filtering algorithm",n:"SIGGRAPH 2025; large kernels / high bit depth",key_findings:"Fast isotropic median filtering removes the classic dependence on bit depth and kernel size, providing edge-preserving smoothing robust to outliers.",limitations:"Purely a filtering primitive; scope is narrow relative to learned image processing."},{ay:"Moroto 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555512",community:12,modality:"Constant-time median filter",n:"SIGGRAPH Asia 2022; 2D wavelet matrix",key_findings:"A 2D wavelet-matrix formulation yields constant-time median filtering independent of kernel size for impulse-noise removal and restoration.",limitations:"Constant factors and memory can be significant; benefits are kernel-size and hardware dependent."}],t={eras:[{period:"2021-2022",title:"Neural fields and neural appearance",dominant_question:"Can we reconstruct and render real scenes with neural representations?",description:"Neural radiance fields matured into practical reconstruction, including dynamic scenes via time-aware neural voxels (Fang 2022) and free-viewpoint video (Lin 2021). In parallel, rendering research began learning appearance and making renderers differentiable (Bangaru 2022; Zeltner 2023), setting up the shift from hand-built pipelines to optimized, learned scene representations.",key_papers:[{ay:"Fang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555383"},{ay:"Lin 2021",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555376"},{ay:"Bangaru 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555397"}]},{period:"2022-2023",title:"Diffusion priors enter graphics",dominant_question:"Can pretrained 2D diffusion/CLIP priors drive graphics content creation?",description:"Pretrained image priors became engines for graphics: zero-shot text-to-mesh (Khalid 2022), text-driven neural-field editing (Zhuang 2023), and personalization without test-time fine-tuning (Ma 2023, Subject-Diffusion), while diffusion reached 3D shape generation in the wavelet domain (Hui 2022). The question shifted from 'how do we model this?' to 'how do we condition a powerful prior?'",key_papers:[{ay:"Khalid 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555392"},{ay:"Zhuang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3610548.3618190"},{ay:"Ma 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657469"},{ay:"Hui 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555394"}]},{period:"2023-2024",title:"The Gaussian-splatting turn",dominant_question:"Can an explicit, real-time representation beat implicit NeRF?",description:"3D Gaussian Splatting reset the reconstruction field toward explicit primitives, and the community raced to fix its weaknesses: geometric accuracy via 2D Gaussians and surfels (Huang 2024; Dai 2024), dynamic 4D scenes (Duan 2024), and physical interactivity (Jiang 2024). Explicit, real-time, editable representations displaced implicit fields for most novel-view synthesis.",key_papers:[{ay:"Huang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657428"},{ay:"Dai 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657441"},{ay:"Duan 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657463"},{ay:"Jiang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657448"}]},{period:"2024-2025",title:"Generative video, 4D, and large 3D-asset models",dominant_question:"Can we generate production-scale, controllable 3D/4D content?",description:"The generative turn peaked: controllable text-to-video and image-to-video (Wang 2023; Shi 2024), whole-clip space-time diffusion (Bar-Tal 2024), few-step distillation for speed (Sauer 2024), and large controllable 3D generators of geometry and materials (Zhang 2024). Controllability, temporal consistency, and inference cost became the central battlegrounds.",key_papers:[{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657518"},{ay:"Bar-Tal 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Sauer 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Zhang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658146"}]},{period:"2022-2025",title:"The persistent physics-and-light-transport core",dominant_question:"Do first-principles rendering and simulation still lead on fidelity and robustness?",description:"Running throughout the era, the classical core kept setting the bar: unconditionally stable, intersection-free solvers for deformables and contact (Chen 2024; Huang 2023), the flow-map paradigm for accurate fluids (Zhou 2024), and physically-based inverse rendering (Wang 2023, ReSTIR). These results anchored the fidelity and robustness that learned methods are benchmarked against.",key_papers:[{ay:"Chen 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658179"},{ay:"Huang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3643028"},{ay:"Zhou 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658180"},{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618331"}]}],debates:[{name:"Explicit Gaussian splatting vs implicit neural fields",side_a:"Explicit Gaussian primitives render in real time and are easy to edit and manipulate.",side_b:"Implicit neural fields represent continuous surfaces and view-dependent effects more faithfully.",description:"3D/2D Gaussian splatting largely won on speed and editability, but its explicit, disconnected primitives are geometrically loose, prompting surfel and opacity-field hybrids that reintroduce surface accuracy. The debate is settling toward explicit-for-speed with structure added back in.",status:"partial consensus",key_papers:[{ay:"Huang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657428"},{ay:"Dai 2024",doi:"10.1145/3641519.3657441"},{ay:"Fang 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555383"}]},{name:"Neural/learned appearance vs unbiased Monte Carlo rendering",side_a:"Learned neural appearance and decoders bring complex materials to real-time rates.",side_b:"Physically-based Monte Carlo light transport remains the unbiased ground-truth reference.",description:"Rather than one replacing the other, the field is converging on hybrids: neural appearance models for interactive rendering, physically-based and differentiable estimators (ReSTIR, differentiable path integrals) for correctness and inverse problems. The reference standard stays Monte Carlo.",status:"reframed",key_papers:[{ay:"Zeltner 2023",doi:"10.1145/3659577"},{ay:"Wang 2023",doi:"10.1145/3618331"},{ay:"Bangaru 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550469.3555397"}]},{name:"Diffusion-generated assets vs authored/structured assets",side_a:"Diffusion generators produce photoreal geometry and materials from text or images at scale.",side_b:"Production needs structured, editable, riggable assets, not just photoreal outputs.",description:"Large generators like CLAY produce impressive assets, but editability and structure are the gating requirements; approaches like BrepGen show that generating structured, editable representations (B-rep CAD) is possible but hard. Whether generation can meet authoring standards is unresolved.",status:"unresolved",key_papers:[{ay:"Zhang 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658146"},{ay:"Xu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658129"},{ay:"Wu 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658188"}]},{name:"Learning-based simulation vs first-principles solvers",side_a:"Neural surrogates and reduced-order models promise faster, data-driven simulation.",side_b:"First-principles numerical solvers give accuracy, stability, and guarantees.",description:"Neural cloth, neural flow maps, and neural reduced-order models accelerate simulation, but the most-adopted results of the era are classical solvers (VBD, GIPC). Learning helps as acceleration or priors, while accuracy-critical simulation stays first-principles.",status:"unresolved",key_papers:[{ay:"Bertiche 2022",doi:"10.1145/3550454.3555491"},{ay:"Deng 2023",doi:""},{ay:"Chen 2024",doi:"10.1145/3658179"}]},{name:"Quality vs real-time / resource efficiency",side_a:"Offline, high-sample methods maximize fidelity regardless of cost.",side_b:"Interactive applications demand real-time rendering and cheap inference.",description:"Across rendering and generation, the era's engineering is largely about closing the quality/speed gap: distillation for few-step diffusion (Sauer 2024), pruning and memory reduction for splatting (Mallick 2024), and neural decoders for real-time materials (Zeltner 2023). Partial consensus is emerging that distillation and compression can approach offline quality.",status:"partial consensus",key_papers:[{ay:"Sauer 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Mallick 2024",doi:""},{ay:"Zeltner 2023",doi:"10.1145/3659577"}]}]},o=`## The shape of computer graphics, 2022-2025

Across four years of SIGGRAPH and SIGGRAPH Asia technical papers (1,236 papers grouped into 13 Louvain communities), computer graphics reorganized itself around a single idea: the *learned, differentiable scene representation*. The most-cited communities in the corpus are the newest ones - radiance fields and Gaussian splatting (mean 60.5 citations), diffusion-based image and video generation (53.3), and generative 3D content (25.5) - while the field's classical pillars of physically-based rendering, elastodynamic simulation, geometry processing, and fluids continue at a steadier cadence with lower per-paper citation counts inside this short window. The story of the era is not that neural methods replaced the classics, but that they were bolted onto every subfield at once - from head avatars (Chen 2023) and clothed humans (Lin 2024) to CAD generation (Xu 2024) and cloth (Bertiche 2022) - while the classical core kept setting the fidelity and robustness bar the learned methods are measured against. Below, each of the 13 communities is named for what its members actually are, not the keyword placeholder it was auto-labelled with; several of those placeholders were wrong.

## Radiance fields and the Gaussian-splatting turn

If one paper defines the period it is 2D Gaussian Splatting (Huang 2024), the single most-cited work in the corpus at over 1,500 citations. Building on the 3D Gaussian Splatting breakthrough, this community pivoted almost entirely from implicit neural radiance fields toward *explicit* point-based primitives that render in real time. The cluster reads as a rapid, focused engineering campaign to keep splatting's speed while repairing its weaknesses: flattening 3D Gaussians into surfels for accurate geometry (Dai 2024), reconstructing surfaces via opacity fields (Yu 2024), extending splatting to dynamic 4D scenes (Duan 2024; Fang 2022), scaling to city-sized captures with a level-of-detail hierarchy (Kerbl 2024), taming memory and runaway Gaussian counts (Mallick 2024), sorting for view-consistency (Radl 2024), and even ray-tracing the particles for reflections and secondary effects (Moenne-Loccoz 2024). The residual NeRF lineage persists for free-viewpoint video (Lin 2021) and walkable VR spaces (Xu 2023, VR-NeRF), and reflection-aware point methods (Kopanas 2022) and casual monocular capture (Stearns 2024) round out the range. The recurring tension - explicit splats are fast but geometrically loose, implicit fields are accurate but slow - drove the wave of surface-reconstruction hybrids and made physical interactivity a first-class goal (VR-GS, Jiang 2024).

## The generative wave: diffusion for images, video, and 3D

Two communities carry the generative revolution. In 2D, diffusion models moved from single-image personalization and concept extraction (Avrahami 2023; Alaluf 2023; Tewel 2024) to controllable video: MotionCtrl (Wang 2023) disentangles camera and object motion, Direct-a-Video (Yang 2024) gives user-directed camera control, Motion-I2V (Shi 2024) factorizes image-to-video through an explicit motion field, and Lumiere (Bar-Tal 2024) generates a video's whole temporal extent in one space-time pass. Because inference cost is the recurring obstacle, a parallel thread attacks sampling speed through adversarial diffusion distillation toward single-step synthesis (Sauer 2024). Crucially, diffusion also re-entered rendering itself: RGB<->X (Zeng 2024) unifies forward rendering, per-pixel inverse rendering, and image synthesis in one diffusion architecture, and Diffusion as Shader (Gu 2025) makes video diffusion 3D-aware. In 3D, the generative-shape community - mislabelled "cages/barycentric" - grew from CLIP-Mesh's zero-shot text-to-mesh (Khalid 2022) to CLAY (Zhang 2024), a large-scale controllable generator of geometry and PBR materials, plus expandable scene synthesis (Wu 2024, BlockFusion), text-driven neural-field editing (Zhuang 2023, DreamEditor), garment generation from text (He 2024, DressCode), PBR-aware texturing (Zhang 2024, DreamMat; Yu 2024, TEXGen), and part-aware single-view reconstruction (Liu 2024, Part123). The through-line is that a pretrained 2D prior has become a reusable engine for 3D and 4D content.

## Digital humans: avatars, faces, motion, and garments

Three communities specialize in people, and all three were reshaped by the neural turn. Head avatars migrated from morphable-mesh and facial-NeRF models (Gao 2022; Zhang 2022) to Gaussian point-based heads and blendshapes (Chen 2023; Ma 2024; Kirschstein 2024, GGHead; Giebenhain 2024, NPGA) and universal relightable codec avatars (Li 2024, URAvatar), while speech-driven facial animation adopted diffusion and multi-modal guidance (Sun 2023, DiffPoseTalk; Zhao 2024, Media2Face) and lip-sync editing matured in the wild (Cheng 2022, VideoReTalking). Character animation split between physics-based control - reinforcement-learned controllers unified under masked motion inpainting (Tessler 2024, MaskedMimic), scalable discrete motion representations (Yao 2023, MoConVQ), and conditional adversarial skill embeddings (Dou 2023, C.ASE) - and kinematic generation, where diffusion now handles in-betweening (Cohan 2024), text-driven motion editing (Athanasiou 2024, MotionFix), co-speech gesture (Ao 2022; Zhang 2024, Semantic Gesticulator), and human-object interaction (Li 2023; Christen 2024, DiffH2O), while sparse-sensor tracking runs in real time from a few IMUs (Jiang 2022) or an HMD and controllers (Winkler 2022, QuestSim). Biomechanically accurate skeletons (Keller 2023) and robust hand tracking (Han 2022, UmeTrack) anchor the capture side. Clothed avatars and garments form their own cluster, spanning monocular body-and-clothing capture (Feng 2022), programmatic sewing patterns (Korosteleva 2023, GarmentCode), single-image sewing-pattern recovery (Liu 2023) and human digitization via shape-guided diffusion (AlBahar 2023), layered Gaussian avatars that transfer clothing across identities (Lin 2024, LayGA), physically-simulated clothing appearance (Xiang 2022, Dressing Avatars), and relightable full-body codec avatars (Wang 2025).

## The enduring core: light transport, simulation, and geometry

The classical heart of graphics did not stand still. The rendering community advanced physically-based Monte Carlo and differentiable rendering: correct gradients for neural SDF renderers (Bangaru 2022), warped-area reparameterization of differential path integrals and projective sampling for geometry (Zhang 2023), reservoir resampling for physics-based inverse rendering (Wang 2023, ReSTIR), grid-free Monte Carlo and walk-on-spheres estimators for PDEs and even fluids (Rioux-Lavoie 2022), differentiable shader programming infrastructure (Bangaru 2023, SLANG.D), measured SVBRDF material capture and generation (Zhou 2022, TileGen; Ma 2023, OpenSVBRDF), and real-time neural appearance models that bring offline-quality materials to interactive rates (Zeltner 2023). Elastodynamic simulation produced some of the most practically important solvers of the era - Vertex Block Descent (Chen 2024) for unconditionally stable, massively parallel implicit integration, and GIPC (Huang 2023) for fast, intersection-free IPC contact - alongside representation-agnostic elasticity (Modi 2024, Simplicits), GPU projective dynamics for cloth (Li 2023), learned cloth dynamics and intersection resolution (Bertiche 2022; Grigorev 2024, ContourCraft), inverse material and metamaterial design (Ren 2024), and a computational-fabrication strand on multi-axis 3D-print slicing (Liu 2024; Zhang 2022, S3-Slicer). Geometry processing kept refining surface reconstruction and CAD: statistical Poisson reconstruction (Sellan 2022), neural Galerkin solvers (Huang 2022), implicit representation of unoriented point clouds via singular-Hessian regularization (Wang 2023), robust mesh Booleans (Cherchi 2022), constructive solid geometry on neural SDFs (Marschner 2023), and a fast-growing generative-CAD strand producing editable B-rep models (Xu 2024, BrepGen; Liu 2025, HoLa) and 3D shapes in the wavelet domain (Hui 2022). Fluids advanced almost entirely through the flow-map paradigm - neural flow maps (Deng 2023) and particle flow maps (Zhou 2024) for accurate long-range advection, Eulerian vortex methods on flow maps (Wang 2024), and covector/coadjoint formulations (Li 2024; Nabizadeh 2024) - plus implicit SPH surface tension (Jeske 2023), hybrid Lagrangian/Eulerian inelastic flows (Qu 2023), and neural reduced-order elastoplasticity and fracture (Zong 2023; Chang 2023, LiCROM).

## Displays, optics, perception, and the long tail

A quieter but distinctive community works at the hardware-perception boundary. Computer-generated holography advanced brightness and realism through multi-color driving schemes (Kavakli 2023), pupil-aware optimization (Chakravarthula 2022), depolarized holography with metasurfaces (Nam 2023), and holographic parallax for perceived 3D realism (Kim 2024). Co-designed computational cameras and optics tackled snapshot hyperspectral imaging (Shi 2024), split-aperture 2-in-1 sensing (Shi 2024), thin on-sensor nanophotonic arrays (Chakravarthula 2023), and end-to-end refractive-diffractive lens design (Yang 2024). Perception and displays contributed color-and-video visual-difference prediction (Mantiuk 2024, ColorVideoVDP), color-perception-guided VR power reduction (Duinkharjav 2022), realistic VR luminance (Matsuda 2022), and cybersickness mitigation (Groth 2024), while a sampling sub-thread produced Gaussian blue noise (Ahmed 2022) and filtered sliced optimal-transport sampling (Salaun 2022). A small but high-impact intrinsic-imaging and relighting cluster separates images into albedo, shading, and illumination for editing and compositing, moving from optimization and differentiable Monte Carlo inverse rendering (Zhu 2022; Li 2022, NeuLighting) to ordinal-shading decomposition (Careaga 2023), diffusion-based intrinsic layers and normals (Luo 2024; Careaga 2024; Ye 2024, StableNormal), and controllable relighting and shadow removal (Magar 2025, LightLab; Yoon 2024). Finally, the corpus contains a tiny but telling island of pure algorithmics - constant-time, isotropic, and parallel-tiled median filtering (Moroto 2022; Weiss 2025; Sugy 2025) - a reminder that classical, non-learned performance work still earns a place at the top venues.

## Open debates

Several genuine tensions run through the corpus. Explicit Gaussian splatting versus implicit neural fields is largely settled on speed but still contested on surface accuracy, which is why so much of the splatting cluster is surfel and opacity-field hybrids that reintroduce structure (Dai 2024; Yu 2024). Neural appearance versus unbiased Monte Carlo rendering is being reframed rather than won: learned decoders deliver real-time complex materials (Zeltner 2023) while physically-based and differentiable estimators remain the ground-truth reference and keep improving (Wang 2023, ReSTIR; Bangaru 2022). The sharpest open question is whether diffusion-generated assets can become production-ready: CLAY (Zhang 2024) produces stunning geometry, but structured, editable outputs (Xu 2024, BrepGen) and physical controllability (Jiang 2024, VR-GS) remain the gating requirements. Learning-based simulation continues to trail first-principles solvers on accuracy and guarantees - the most-adopted simulation results of the era (Chen 2024; Huang 2023) are classical numerics, not neural surrogates, with learning entering as acceleration or priors (Deng 2023; Zong 2023). And across rendering and generation, the quality-versus-real-time axis frames much of the engineering, resolved incrementally through distillation (Sauer 2024) and pruning (Mallick 2024).

## Outlook

The trajectory points toward convergence: differentiable rendering already couples optimization to image formation, and the next frontier is making learned representations *simulatable and editable* rather than merely viewable. Bridges already exist - Simplicits (Modi 2024) simulates any representation, VR-GS (Jiang 2024) gives splats physical dynamics, and RGB<->X (Zeng 2024) folds inverse rendering into a generative model - but the generative and simulation communities in this corpus still cite each other sparingly, and their citation profiles reveal the split: the neural clusters are young and heavily cited, the simulation clusters older-rooted and steadier. Closing that gap, so that a single asset can be generated, relit, rigged, simulated, and animated without expensive manual conversion, is the defining challenge the field is walking into - and the papers that already straddle the divide are the ones to watch.`,r={schools:e,gap:i,argument_spine:a,evidence:n,debate:t,review_markdown:o};export{a as argument_spine,t as debate,r as default,n as evidence,i as gap,o as review_markdown,e as schools};
